# Market data vendor (prices, fundamentals, statements) — https://twelvedata.com
# ADX and DFM publish no public data feed, so quotes come from this licensed vendor. Without a key the
# markets pages still list every ADX/DFM stock and show DFM filings, but prices/indicators show "not connected".
TWELVEDATA_API_KEY=
# Requests per minute allowed by your plan (free = 8). Raise it on paid plans so the board loads faster.
TWELVEDATA_RPM=8
# Dev only: synthetic, clearly-labelled test data so the UI can be developed without a key. Ignored in production.
# GD_FIXTURES=1

# AI research tab. Credentials resolve in this order: ANTHROPIC_API_KEY, ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN, or your `ant auth login` profile
# (a profile is already active on this machine, so nothing is needed in dev). Each note bills your Anthropic account.
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# RESEARCH_MODEL=claude-sonnet-5-5   # default; Opus costs about twice as much per token
# RESEARCH_EFFORT=medium             # low | medium | high | xhigh | max
# RESEARCH_MAX_RUN_USD=1             # hard ceiling per note in US dollars (default 1, never above 5)
# RESEARCH_MAX_PER_HOUR=6            # server-wide cap on new notes
# RESEARCH_ENABLED=0                 # set to 0 to switch the feature off
# AI country briefs (no web tools; about $0.015 each on the default model; cached 3 h; start only on click)
# BRIEF_MODEL=claude-sonnet-5-5
# The country brief and the prep pack cost about 4 and 6 cents on Sonnet. claude-haiku-5-5 cuts that by about 70 percent (1.2 and 1.6 cents) and writes a close second-best, but in testing it once named the wrong weakest aspect of the scorecard, so Sonnet is the default. Set BRIEF_MODEL / PREP_MODEL to try it.
# BRIEF_MAX_PER_HOUR=20              # server-wide cap on new (uncached) briefs
# BRIEF_ENABLED=0                    # set to 0 to switch briefs off
# DOSSIER_MODEL=claude-sonnet-5-5    # detailed ministerial and desk briefings (read the web); Opus costs about twice as much
# DOSSIER_EFFORT=                    # leave empty for low (short runs) or medium (long runs); low | medium | high | xhigh | max
# DOSSIER_MAX_RUN_USD=1              # hard ceiling per briefing run in US dollars (default 1, never above 5)
# DOSSIER_MAX_PER_HOUR=4             # server-wide cap on new detailed briefings
# DOSSIER_ENABLED=0                  # set to 0 to switch them off

# Optional free keys that switch on key-gated layers (each shows a clear message until set)
# AISSTREAM_API_KEY=           # live vessels (AIS): https://aisstream.io
# WINDY_WEBCAMS_API_KEY=       # public webcams: https://api.windy.com/webcams

# Cheaper models for council calls (off by default: every role runs on Claude unless switched here). One role at a time, so you can keep the chief writer and the auditors on Claude.
# BEST FREE START: one free Google AI Studio key (https://aistudio.google.com/apikey, no card) gives a free model AND free Google Search in one call:
#   GEMINI_API_KEY=...   LLM_SITTING=gemini-grounded     (Gemini 2.5 Flash with Google Search grounding: 500 grounded requests a day free)
# Caveats: the free tier may use your prompts to improve Google's products; the model is a Flash model, so run scripts/ab-sitting.ts before trusting it; check your limits at https://aistudio.google.com/rate-limit
# Aliases: gemini-grounded (Gemini 2.5 Flash + Google Search; GEMINI_API_KEY), gemini-flash (Gemini 3.8 Flash, free tokens, uses Geo Desk's own search; GEMINI_API_KEY), groq-gpt-oss (GROQ_API_KEY, free tier, fast),
#   or-nemotron-ultra, or-gemma (OPENROUTER_API_KEY, free models, rate-limited, provider may log prompts), hf-deepseek-flash, hf-deepseek-pro, hf-qwen, hf-gpt-oss (HF_TOKEN with Inference Providers credit),
#   deepseek-flash, deepseek-pro (DEEPSEEK_API_KEY, paid but cheap). An unknown alias or a missing key means Claude.
# LLM_SITTING=gemini-grounded        # the specialist sittings, about 70 percent of a council's cost
# LLM_CHIEF=claude                   # the chief writer
# LLM_AUDIT=claude                   # the two auditors (a different vendor's model checking Claude's work is also a good independence test)
# LLM_FALLBACK=1                     # 1 (default): a provider failure re-runs that call on Claude. 0: show the failure
# GEMINI_API_KEY=                    # free; GEMINI_MODEL overrides the model id for gemini-grounded (default gemini-2.5-flash)
# GROQ_API_KEY=  OPENROUTER_API_KEY=  HF_TOKEN=  DEEPSEEK_API_KEY=
# Web search for the models that have none of their own (everything except gemini-grounded). Every key you add joins a rotation, so free quotas last longer; a provider that runs out is left alone for an hour and the keyless search takes over if all fail.
# TAVILY_API_KEY=                    # https://tavily.com   1,000 searches a month, no card
# LINKUP_API_KEY=                    # https://linkup.so    about 20 euros of credit at signup, topped up monthly, no card
# EXA_API_KEY=                       # https://exa.ai       10 dollars of credit a month, no card
# SERPER_API_KEY=                    # https://serper.dev   2,500 Google queries once
# BRAVE_API_KEY=                     # https://brave.com/search/api   now billed per request and needs a card
# (limits are from third-party comparisons dated 27 Oct 2026 and change often; confirm on each site. Without any key a thin keyless search over news, think-tank and official feeds, GDELT, Wikipedia, World Bank documents and Marginalia is used, and pages that will not read are tried through Jina Reader, free without a key.)
